# CeramicTiles : Julien Delannoy ceramic tiles in Houdini Copernicus (2 October 2026)

One Copernicus graph, `CeramicTiles.hiplc` (network `/obj/CeramicGreen_Height`, 140 nodes), makes the six final maps of FOUR tile patterns. The HDA parameter `variant` of the master network switches between them (2 October 2026).

| `variant` | Pattern | Reference | Maps folder | Folder of its parameters |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| 0 | 01a green lenses (the original graph, untouched, bit for bit) | `ref/01a-julien-delannoy-10-left.png` | `maps/01a_green_lenses/` | the original `HDA` folders |
| 1 | 01b pillow tiles, 6 x 6 cushions with star voids | `ref/01b-julien-delannoy-10-right.png` | `maps/01b_pillow_tiles/` | `HDA 01b Pillow` (8 parameters, prefix `v1_`) |
| 2 | 02a serpentine arcs, 5 x 5 Truchet tiles | `ref/02a-julien-delannoy-11-left.png` | `maps/02a_serpentine_arcs/` | `HDA 02a Serpentine` (8 parameters, prefix `v2_`) |
| 3 | 02b terracotta bowls, 6 x 6 tiles | `ref/02b-julien-delannoy-11-right.png` | `maps/02b_terracotta_bowls/` | `HDA 02b Terracotta` (8 parameters, prefix `v3_`) |

Each `maps/<variant>/` holds `height, normal, basecolor, roughness, ao, reflect` (PNG) and a `preview.png` sheet (reference, relit maps, basecolor, height, normal).

## The two phase rule (2 October 2026)

Every variant is built twice. Phase 1 explores in layers, one wrangle per stage (up to 64 nodes) until the look is right. Phase 2 fuses the layers into ONE wrangle per map (7 nodes per variant) and the six maps must stay identical (maxdiff 0.0, proven for 01b, 02a, 02b). The whole graph stays under 150 nodes.

