## Scripts of the variant work

| Script | Role |
|---|---|
| `Scripts/V2Infra.py` | adds the `variant` menu, the six switches `SW_n_*` and the six export ROPs `VX_export__*` (idempotent) |
| `Scripts/VariantLib.py`, `Scripts/VariantEngine.py` | helpers and the stage engine: a map is a list of VEX stages on a running vector `S`, built layered or fused |
| `Scripts/Variant01b.py`, `Variant02a.py`, `Variant02b.py` | one file per variant: parameters (`SPECS`), pattern prelude, stages |
| `Scripts/BuildVariant.py <hip in> <hip out> <01b\|02a\|02b> <layered\|fused> [--reset-params]` | builds one variant into a hip |
| `Scripts/CookVariant.py <hip> <variant> <res> <outdir>` | cooks the six maps of one variant headless |
| `Scripts/ExportVariantMaps.sh <hip> [res] [exposure]` | exports the four variants into `maps/` with previews |
| `Scripts/PreviewVariant.py` | side by side sheet, reference against relit maps |
| `Scripts/NonRegression01a.py <hip> [res]` | gate: variant 0 must equal the original graph (exit code 1 if not) |
| `Scripts/TidyVariants.py` | lays out the variant bands and boxes them |
| `Scripts/Fit01b.py`, `Fit02a.py`, `Fit02b.py` | measure each reference (tile grid, orientations, colours) into `ref-maps/` |
| `Scripts/RepointHip.py` | rewrites the project paths of a hip after a move |

## Colour rule of the variants

The export applies the sRGB curve, so every colour constant measured on a PNG reference is converted with `srgb2lin` (helper `lin3()` in the variant code) before it enters the stages. Forgetting it gives pale maps (found and fixed on 01b and 02a, 2 October 2026).

